{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/Developer/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk/usr/share/man/man2/rename.2 | sed -n '125,157p;225,263p'\"","aggregated_output":"   125\t.Fa flags\n   126\targument.\n   127\tValues for\n   128\t.Fa flags\n   129\tare constructed with below bits set:\n   130\t.Bl -tag -width VOL_CAP_INT_RENAME_EXCL\n   131\t.It Dv RENAME_SWAP\n   132\tOn file systems that support it (see\n   133\t.Xr getattrlist 2\n   134\t.Dv VOL_CAP_INT_RENAME_SWAP Ns ),\n   135\tit will cause the source and target to be atomically swapped.  Source and target need not be of\n   136\tthe same type, i.e. it is possible to swap a file with a directory.\n   137\tEINVAL is returned in case of bitwise-inclusive OR with\n   138\t.Dv RENAME_EXCL .\n   139\t.It Dv RENAME_EXCL\n   140\tOn file systems that support it (see\n   141\t.Xr getattrlist 2\n   142\t.Dv VOL_CAP_INT_RENAME_EXCL Ns ),\n   143\tit will cause\n   144\t.Dv EEXIST\n   145\tto be returned if the destination already exists. EINVAL is returned in case of bitwise-inclusive OR with\n   146\t.Dv RENAME_SWAP .\n   147\t.It Dv RENAME_NOFOLLOW_ANY\n   148\tIf any symbolic links are encountered during pathname resolution, an error is returned.\n   149\t.It Dv RENAME_RESOLVE_BENEATH\n   150\tEither\n   151\t.Fa from\n   152\tor\n   153\t.Fa to\n   154\tdoes not reside in the hierarchy beneath the starting directory,\n   155\tan error is returned.\n   156\t.El\n   157\t.Sh CAVEATS\n   225\tThe directory in which the entry for the new name\n   226\tis being placed cannot be extended because the\n   227\tuser's quota of disk blocks on the file system\n   228\tcontaining the directory has been exhausted.\n   229\t.\\\" ===========\n   230\t.It Bq Er EEXIST\n   231\t.Fa flags\n   232\thas\n   233\t.Dv RENAME_EXCL\n   234\tset but\n   235\t.Fa new\n   236\talready exists.\n   237\t.\\\" ===========\n   238\t.It Bq Er EFAULT\n   239\t.Em Path\n   240\tpoints outside the process's allocated address space.\n   241\t.\\\" ===========\n   242\t.It Bq Er EINVAL\n   243\t.Fa Old\n   244\tis a parent directory of\n   245\t.Fa new ,\n   246\tor an attempt is made to rename\n   247\t.Ql \\&.\n   248\tor\n   249\t.Ql \\&.. .\n   250\tIf\n   251\t.Dv RENAME_SWAP\n   252\tis used, then\n   253\t.Dv EINVAL\n   254\twill also be returned if\n   255\t.Fa new\n   256\tis a parent directory of\n   257\t.Fa old .\n   258\tIf both RENAME_SWAP and RENAME_EXCL bits are set in\n   259\t.Fa flags ,\n   260\tthen\n   261\t.Dv EINVAL\n   262\twill be returned.\n   263\t.\\\" ===========\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build.** Revision 5 closes both 74d defects at `--out`. Two issues remain. Test 14 checks the command’s exit status on the wrong path, and cleanup can delete a directory that reuses the staging name after publication.\n\n1. **Both 74d defects are closed in the design.** The only operation that creates `--out` is an atomic move that refuses an existing destination, including an empty directory. A database error before that move leaves only private staging to clean up. Test 17 specifies the missing-table error, exit 1, absence of both output and staging, and a successful retry at the same path. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:142) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:171](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:171) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:329](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:329)\n\n2. **Test 14 still misses the command’s late refusal.** Its module test creates the foreign empty directory after staging. Its command test creates the directory before startup, so the early check can return exit 1 without ever reaching `publish` or staging cleanup. Run the real command on a scratch copy with a pause immediately before `publish`, create the empty directory, then resume. Assert exit 1, removal of the build’s staging folder, and survival of the same empty directory by device and inode. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:161](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:161) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:212) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:326](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:326) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:328](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:328)\n\n3. **Revision 5 introduces a cleanup race at the old staging name.** Once `publish` succeeds, the rename frees that name. If another process creates a directory there before `finally` runs, the specified “if it still exists” check can remove the new directory. End the build’s cleanup responsibility as soon as the move succeeds. The decisive test recreates the old staging directory with a marker file after the move and verifies that the marker survives command exit. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:138](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:138) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:163](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:163) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:167)"}}
